# man - show the manual page of a command or program

## SYNOPSIS
    man [-a] [-w] [-L LANG] NAME ...
    man -k WORD
    man -l FILE

## DESCRIPTION
Shows the manual page for NAME. In a window it opens the page in its own
viewer: scroll, search, and **q** to quit. When the output goes to a file
or a pipe the page comes out as plain text, so `man ls | grep -i sort`
works.

man finds pages in this order, and the first one wins:

    MAN:LANG/PROGRAM/NAME.man         pages installed for programs
    HELP:LANG/Sys/DRAWER/NAME.help    the system's own pages (3.2)
    the same two in english
    NAME.guide or NAME.doc            next to the program, or in HELP:

LANG is the language chosen in Locale prefs (english without
locale.library). MAN: is an assign: on AmigaOS 3.x it usually points to
HELP:Man, on older systems to SYS:Man. Add your own pages with
`Assign MAN: Work:MyPages ADD` and put them in
`Work:MyPages/english/Mine/NAME.man`.

Pages may be .man files (marked-up text, see `docs/man.md`), plain text
in the manual's own form (NAME, FORMAT, TEMPLATE...), or AmigaGuide.

## OPTIONS
- **-a** every page found for NAME, one after another, not only the
  first.
- **-w** where the page is (its path), not the page.
- **-L** LANG look in another language's pages first, e.g. svenska.
- **-k** WORD list the pages whose name or one-line summary has WORD
  in it (as Unix apropos).
- **-l** FILE show FILE as a page.

## THE VIEWER
- **Down j Return** one line on.
- **Up k** one line back.
- **Space PgDn f** a page on; **b PgUp** a page back.
- **d u** half a page on or back.
- **g Home** the start; **G End** the end.
- **/** search forward, **?** backward; every match is marked.
- **n N** the next match, the one before.
- **h Help** the keys; **q Esc** quit.

The mouse wheel scrolls in CTerm. When the window changes size, the
text is wrapped again to the new width.

## ENVIRONMENT
- **PAGER** another viewer for the pages, e.g. `SetEnv PAGER Maki`.
  The page is handed to it in colour; man's own viewer is not used.

## EXAMPLES
    man ls
    man -k copy
    man -w list
    man -L svenska list
    man grep | grep -i colour
    SetEnv PAGER Maki

## RETURN CODES
0 a page was shown, 5 no page was found, 10 bad arguments, 20 Ctrl-C.

## SEE ALSO
